    "type": "question",
    "label": "5",
    "prompt": "When Mary differentiates functions of the form $y=f(x)g(x)$, she likes to write her working out as $$y'=g'(x)f(x)+f'(x)g(x).$$ Does this matter? Why or why not?",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "No. The product-rule terms can be added in either order.",
      "worked": "No. Since multiplication and addition are commutative, $g'(x)f(x)+f'(x)g(x)=f'(x)g(x)+f(x)g'(x)$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
